<title>UK: Bankgesellschaft adds 100 bln lire to two-yr bond. [CORRECTED 16:10 GMT]</title>
<headline>Bankgesellschaft adds 100 bln lire to two-yr bond. [CORRECTED 16:10 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased, joint lead managers Cariplo and IMI Luxembourg said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BGB FINANCE IRELAND PLC</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  BANKGESELLSCHAFT BERLIN GROUP</p>
<p> AMT  * 350 BLN LIRE  COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    20.NOV.98</p>
<p> TYPE   ZERO-COUPON   ISS PRICE  89.285    PAY DATE    20.NOV.96</p>
<p> (Corrects ISS PRICE from 89.295)</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.125     REOFFER    =	   SPREAD	=</p>
<p> NOTES    * ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED FOR 250 BLN LIRE ON 31.OCT.96</p>
<p> MOODY	AA1	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (M) 5-50	SALE LIMS US/UK/IT/IR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  0.875</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF AN EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
